    },
    "rich_text_6ghwNj": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_4hYRP3": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading_text": "What the Root Analysis Service includes",
            "heading_size": "h2",
            "enable_h1_tag": false
          }
        },
        "description_CwddzY": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description_text": "<p>Our Root Analysis Service is designed specifically for truffle orchards—using methods refined across ATC’s network of orchards in North America and in collaboration with global research partners. <strong>Subtleties in how the mycorrhiza manifests itself can mean the difference in distinguishing the intended mycorrhiza from competing ones.</strong> We bring <strong>20+ years of experience in meticulously analyzing roots </strong>with mycorrhiza to ensure accurate and correct results.</p><p>It is <strong>a yearly microscope- and data-driven health check for your truffle roots. </strong>The quality of this type of root analysis in North America varies widely, because most American academic and even university laboratories lack the extensive knowledge and experience working with <em>Tuber melanosporum</em>. Our expertise and experience in root analysis are based on 20+ years of specializing in <em>T. melanosporum.</em></p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_4hYRP3",
        "description_CwddzY"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.rich_text.name",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "",
